# Gary Gigabytes: Cursor AI Agent Rules

## Project Identity

**What It Is:**
- Jekyll 4.3 static site + personal portfolio + technical blog
- Hugo-like content collections: `_posts/` (blog), `_projects/` (projects), `_csumb/` (courses)
- Hosted on Google Cloud Run (us-central1) with Global Load Balancer + Cloudflare DNS
- Vanilla CSS (dark-mode-first, no frameworks), minimal JavaScript
- Infrastructure: Docker, GitHub Actions CI/CD, Google Cloud Platform

**Key Technologies:**
- Frontend: Jekyll 4.3, Liquid templates, vanilla CSS
- Backend: Docker (multi-stage build), Cloud Run (serverless)
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions (lint + build + deploy)
- Hosting: Google Cloud Run, Global Load Balancer, Cloudflare DNS
- Owner Background: Aerospace ME → CSUMB CS (focus on robotics, autonomous systems, AI/ML)

## Content Conventions

### Collections & Front-Matter

**Blog Posts** (`_posts/YYYY-MM-DD-title.md`):
```yaml
---
layout: post
title: "Title"
date: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [tag1, tag2]
excerpt: Brief summary <!--more--> (marks archive cutoff)
---
```

**Projects** (`_projects/name.md`):
```yaml
---
layout: project
title: "Project Name"
date: YYYY-MM-DD
description: "One-line summary"
tags: [category, tech]
image: /assets/imgs/project/name.png
github: "https://github.com/org/repo"
demo: "https://url"
---
```

**Courses** (`_csumb/cstXXX.md`):
```yaml
---
layout: course
title: "Course Title (CST XXX)"
course: "CSUMB CST XXX"
semester: "Fall 2025"
description: "Summary and learnings"
tags: [csumb, subject]
---
```

### Tag Taxonomy

Common tags (see `_data/tag_links.yml`):
- Courses: `cst300`, `cst499`, `csumb`
- Projects: `hobby-projects`, `capstone`, `research`
- Tech: `robotics`, `marl`, `autonomous-systems`, `ml`, `isaac-lab`, `skrl`
- Specific: `ggswarm`, `hexmaster`, `smart-mirror`, `gary-gigabytes`

### Excerpt Separator

Use `<!--more-->` to mark where the blog archive summary cuts off. Content after this is only shown on the full post page.

## Directory Map

```
ggbsite/
├── _posts/              # Blog posts (Markdown, Jekyll collection)
├── _projects/           # Project showcases (custom collection)
├── _csumb/              # Course documentation (custom collection)
├── _layouts/            # HTML/Liquid templates (post, project, course, default)
├── _includes/           # Reusable components (header, nav, footer, cards, etc.)
├── assets/css/          # Vanilla CSS (dark-mode-first, no frameworks)
├── assets/js/           # Minimal JavaScript
├── assets/imgs/         # Images (organize by category: project/, smartmirror/, etc.)
├── _data/               # YAML data (tag_links.yml for tag taxonomy)
├── .github/workflows/   # GitHub Actions (deploy.yml, lint.yml)
├── Dockerfile           # Multi-stage build: Jekyll build → nginx serve
├── Gemfile              # Ruby dependencies (Jekyll, etc.)
├── _config.yml          # Jekyll config (collections, plugins, excerpts)
├── DEPLOYMENT.md        # GCP Cloud Run operations guide
├── CLOUD_RUN_SETUP.md   # One-time infrastructure bootstrap
├── AGENTS.md            # AI agent context (read first!)
└── README.md            # Project overview + deployment links
```

## Deployment Pipeline

1. **Local:** Write markdown in `_posts/`, `_projects/`, or `_csumb/`
2. **Push:** Commit to `publish` branch
3. **GitHub Actions:** Triggers `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
4. **Build:** `gcloud builds submit` → builds Dockerfile → pushes to GCR
5. **Deploy:** `gcloud run deploy ggbsite` → Cloud Run (us-central1)
6. **Route:** Global Load Balancer (34.36.126.59) → Cloudflare → User

**Current GCP Details:**
- Project: `gary-gigabytes`
- Region: `us-central1`
- Static IP: `34.36.126.59`
- LB URL Map: `gary-gigabytes-urlmap`

## Style Persona

**Voice:** Authentic, Analytical, Visually Descriptive

**Writing Guidelines:**
- **Technical Precision:** Bullet points for mechanics, active language, stay conversational
- **Casual Tone:** Use relatable asides ("Not my proudest moment...") and light markers
- **Vibrant Language:** Active verbs, focus on the "vibe" and energy, avoid corporate speak
- **Formatting:** Mix technical depth with punchy sentences; no long academic paragraphs

## Technical Rules

- **Docker Compose:** Never include `version` field (Compose V2 deprecated syntax)
- **Deployment:** Use GCR-built images for production (Cloud Build from local source)
- **Python (if used):** Strict PEP 8 (Black/Ruff, 88-100 char lines, snake_case filenames)
- **Ruby:** RuboCop enforced (see `.rubocop.yml`)
- **YAML:** yamllint enforced (see `.yamllint.yml`)
- **Markdown:** markdownlint enforced (see `.markdownlint-cli2.yaml`)
- **Dockerfile:** hadolint enforced (see `.hadolint.yaml`)
- **CSS:** Vanilla only, dark-mode-first, no frameworks
- **JavaScript:** Minimal, vanilla (no jQuery)

## How to Add Content

**New Blog Post:**
1. Create `_posts/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`
2. Add front-matter (layout: post, title, date, tags)
3. Use `<!--more-->` to mark archive cutoff
4. Push to `publish` → auto-deploys

**New Project:**
1. Create `_projects/slug.md`
2. Add front-matter (description, tags, image, github link)
3. Write Markdown content
4. Push → auto-deploys

**New Course:**
1. Create `_csumb/cstXXX.md`
2. Add front-matter (course, semester, description, tags)
3. List learnings & links
4. Push → auto-deploys

## Key Files for AI Agents

| File | Purpose | Edit When |
|------|---------|-----------|
| `_config.yml` | Jekyll config, collections, plugins | Adding collection type |
| `_layouts/*.html` | HTML templates (post, project, course) | Changing page structure |
| `_includes/*.html` | Reusable components (nav, footer, cards) | Updating UI elements |
| `assets/css/styles.css` | Vanilla CSS (dark-mode) | Visual updates |
| `.rubocop.yml` | Ruby linting rules | Adjusting code standards |
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | CI/CD pipeline | Changing build/deploy process |
| `Dockerfile` | Container definition | Base image, build steps |
| `_data/tag_links.yml` | Tag taxonomy | Adding new tags or categories |

